  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Naringenin 7-O-(2'',6''-di-O-alpha-rhamnopyranosyl)-beta-glucopyranoside and Tankyrase-2, as this compound is identified as a target of multiple substances that in turn target Tankyrase-2. Specifically, the compound is linked to MIP, which is a target of sodium;(2R,3R)-2,3-dihydroxybutanedioic acid;hydrogen carbonate and sec-Butyl acetate, (-), both of which are known to interact with Tankyrase-2. This indicates a possible pathway where Naringenin 7-O-(2'',6''-di-O-alpha-rhamnopyranosyl)-beta-glucopyranoside may act as a mediator in the interaction with Tankyrase-2, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, suggesting a plausible biological connection, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
